      "id": "6614bd557a85-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Three of the following word pairs are alike in some manner and hence form a group. Which word pair does not belong to that group? (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be grouped based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Three of the following word pairs are alike in some manner and hence form a group. Which word pair does not belong to that group? </p><p>(The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be grouped based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Moon - Night",
          "html": "Moon  -  Night"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Sun - Day",
          "html": "Sun  -  Day"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Rainbow - Rain",
          "html": "Rainbow  -  Rain"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Clouds - Star",
          "html": "Clouds  -  Star"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Moon is visible at night </p><p>Sun appears in a day </p><p>Rainbow occurs in the presence of rain. </p><p>But there is no connection between clouds and stars. Thus, option (d) is odd from the rest. </p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
