      "id": "6614bd557a85-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "The question contains pair of words that are related to each other in a certain way. Three of the following four word pairs are alike as these have the same relationship and thus form a group. Which word pair is the one that DOES NOT belong to that group? (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>The question contains pair of words that are related to each other in a certain way. Three of the following four word pairs are alike as these have the same relationship and thus form a group. Which word pair is the one that DOES NOT belong to that group? </p><p>(The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word)</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Demonstrate - Reveal",
          "html": "Demonstrate  -  Reveal"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Think - Evaluate",
          "html": "Think  -  Evaluate"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Effective - Beneficial",
          "html": "Effective  -  Beneficial"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Loss - Recovery",
          "html": "Loss  -  Recovery"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>The synonym of Demonstrate is Reveal.</p><p>The synonym of Think is Evaluate.</p><p>The synonym of Effective is Beneficial.</p><p>But Recovery is not the synonym of Loss. </p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
